@Emily Wachowiak @Crystal Wong @Jeffrey Guerrero @Tiffanie Shakespearewhat do y'all think of this solution. 

This way, users can just see a list of all languages, and make a decision whether they want to make that language as always/ never (automatically) tanslate. Or offer to translate as a default. 

This eliminates drop downs, and "save" buttons. Allows for a longer list of languages in the future. This also somewhat follows the existing pattern of Site permissions.

@Emily Wachowiak what do you think of this? 

@Tiffanie Shakespeare suggested this, as we typically don't like to have a menu over the bottom sheet. 

This also gives us more room to explain what some of these settings are!

@Emily Wachowiak @Usama Khanlet me know what y'all think of this. 

I remember us talking about how this feels like a bit of a redundant feature. Could it be grouped all together under one "translation setting" type modal. 

Also to the point that Marco brought up about people thinking that when they uninstall it will do the same as unchecking never/always tranalte. Having these housed under one home, might give user a bit more clarity around it.

@Greg Tatum @Usama Khan @Emily Wachowiak 

This is what the proposed solution for now is. 

It has been approved by my manager Andrew for implementation.

